{# Engagement ladder. Copy must stay consistent with hire-me.njk's own FAQ
   ("How does pricing work?") - three formats plus the free discovery call.
   No dollar figures: exact pricing is only ever agreed on the call. #}
<section class="section section-tight">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Ways to Engage</span>
      <h2>One Operator. A Few Ways to Work Together.</h2>
      <p>Pick the format that matches where you are. Exact scope and pricing are set together on the discovery call, not guessed at here.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tiers">
      <article class="tier-card reveal">
        <span class="tier-num">01</span>
        <h3>Free Discovery Call</h3>
        <p class="tier-meta">Complimentary · 30 minutes</p>
        <p>A focused call to map what's draining your week and whether we're the right fit. You leave with a punch list either way.</p>
        <a class="card-link" href="/booking/">Book the call <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="tier-card reveal">
        <span class="tier-num">02</span>
        <h3>Project Engagement</h3>
        <p class="tier-meta">Fixed-scope · Weeks, not months</p>
        <p>A defined deliverable: a market-entry push, a systems build, an operations fix that needs senior attention now, not a new hire.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="tier-card reveal">
        <span class="tier-num">03</span>
        <h3>Fractional Retainer</h3>
        <p class="tier-meta">Ongoing · Monthly, Chief of Staff or Operations Partner scope</p>
        <p>Recurring senior leverage across calendar, operations, and stakeholder management, without the cost of a full-time hire.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="tier-card reveal">
        <span class="tier-num">04</span>
        <h3>Embedded Executive Assistant</h3>
        <p class="tier-meta">Ongoing · Hourly retainer, 10–20 hrs/week</p>
        <p>Daily support for a single executive: inbox, calendar, travel, and communications, run with the same discipline as the retainers above.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
